Package: namzero-lite
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Raffaele P. Guidi <raffaele.p.guidi@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/raffaeleguidi/namzero-lite
Depends: libasound2 (>= 1.2.0), python3 (>= 3.9), python3-venv, libcap2-bin, bluez, network-manager, sudo, adduser, alsa-utils
Recommends: dnsmasq-base
Description: realtime guitar audio engine for Raspberry Pi (NAM lite)
 namzero-lite is a realtime guitar effect engine for Raspberry Pi Zero 2W
 with an XSONIC XTONE (or any ALSA PCM) as audio interface. It implements
 a fixed effect chain with NAM amp models, cabinet IRs, MIDI footswitch
 control and a local web UI.
 .
 This package installs the engine, the Python web UI and BLE MIDI bridge,
 factory presets and systemd units. User configuration lives in
 /etc/namzero (conffiles) and /var/lib/namzero.
